{"seq":4,"slug":"major-works","title":"马可·奥勒留·major-works","stage":"DONE","category":"marcus-aurelius","categoryLabel":"马可·奥勒留","chapterCount":3,"docCount":6,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/marcus-aurelius/major-works","rating":{"composite":3.72,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.4,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":4,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/famous-people/14_marcus-aurelius/4_major-works","introHtml":"<h1 id=\"代表作\">代表作</h1><p>本卷聚焦马可·奥勒留唯一传世、也是其全部声誉所系的著作——《沉思录》。它是一位罗马皇帝在多瑙河前线、用希腊文写给自己的私人札记，本无标题、本无读者，却成为西方最被广泛阅读的精神经典之一。本卷从三个角度剖析这部著作：它<strong>是什么</strong>（成书与文本）、它<strong>说什么</strong>（核心教诲）、它<strong>为何不朽</strong>（文学品质与传世）。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本卷与兄弟卷的分工\">本卷与兄弟卷的分工</h2><p>本人物（马可·奥勒留）下设六卷，各有侧重，避免重复展开：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>本卷（代表作）</strong>：只聚焦《沉思录》这一文本对象——它的成书、结构、核心教诲、文学品质与传世史。</li>\n<li><a href=\"../life-and-times/\">生平与时代</a>：作者的人生轨迹与帝国背景（《沉思录》的写作处境在此）。</li>\n<li><a href=\"../core-contributions/\">核心贡献</a>：作为&quot;哲学家皇帝&quot;的历史地位与德性典范。</li>\n<li><a href=\"../ideas-and-methods/\">思想与方法</a>：斯多葛哲学体系本身（控制二分、逻各斯、灵魂操练的系统阐述）——本卷遇到这些概念时只点到为止，详解链向此卷。</li>\n<li><a href=\"../influence-and-legacy/\">影响与遗产</a>：《沉思录》对后世斯多葛主义与文化的更广影响。</li>\n<li><a href=\"../controversies-and-appraisal/\">争议与评价</a>：对其思想局限与历史评价的批判性讨论。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>一句话区分：<strong>本卷只回答&quot;《沉思录》这本书&quot;的问题；&quot;斯多葛哲学是什么&quot;去思想与方法卷，&quot;它影响了谁&quot;去影响与遗产卷。</strong></p>\n<h2 id=\"三章结构与推荐路径\">三章结构与推荐路径</h2><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>章</th>\n<th>主题</th>\n<th>回答的问题</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>一</td>\n<td><a href=\"the-book-of-meditations/\">《沉思录》其书</a></td>\n<td>它怎么来的、怎么组织的</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>二</td>\n<td><a href=\"core-teachings/\">核心教诲</a></td>\n<td>它教给人什么</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>三</td>\n<td><a href=\"a-literary-treasure/\">文学瑰宝</a></td>\n<td>它为何能不朽</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>推荐学习路径：<strong>第一章 → 第二章 → 第三章</strong>，先了解文本性质，再进入内容，最后理解其历史命运。</p>\n<ul>\n<li>若只想读懂&quot;这是一本什么书&quot;：读第一章两篇即可。</li>\n<li>若想直接获取人生智慧：可先读第二章 <a href=\"core-teachings/on-self-and-others\">论自我与他人</a> 与 <a href=\"core-teachings/on-life-and-death\">论生与死</a>。</li>\n<li>前置知识：建议先浏览 <a href=\"../ideas-and-methods/\">思想与方法</a> 中的斯多葛基本概念（控制二分、逻各斯），本卷多处以此为前提。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>阅读时请记住贯穿本卷的一条线索：《沉思录》的一切特质——零散、重复、亲切、不朽——都源于它&quot;写给自己、并非为发表&quot;这一根本性质。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-book-of-meditations","title":"《沉思录》其书","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/marcus-aurelius/major-works/the-book-of-meditations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"written-to-himself","title":"写给自己的书","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/marcus-aurelius/major-works/the-book-of-meditations/written-to-himself"},{"seq":2,"slug":"structure-and-themes","title":"结构与主题","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/marcus-aurelius/major-works/the-book-of-meditations/structure-and-themes"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"core-teachings","title":"核心教诲","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/marcus-aurelius/major-works/core-teachings","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"on-self-and-others","title":"论自我与他人","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/marcus-aurelius/major-works/core-teachings/on-self-and-others"},{"seq":2,"slug":"on-life-and-death","title":"论生与死","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/marcus-aurelius/major-works/core-teachings/on-life-and-death"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"a-literary-treasure","title":"文学瑰宝","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/marcus-aurelius/major-works/a-literary-treasure","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"intimate-and-universal","title":"亲切而普世","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/marcus-aurelius/major-works/a-literary-treasure/intimate-and-universal"},{"seq":2,"slug":"an-enduring-classic","title":"不朽的经典","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/marcus-aurelius/major-works/a-literary-treasure/an-enduring-classic"}]}]}